DESCRIPTION >
    Time to a visual (work 063), one row per episode. An episode ends at a fact: `file.posted` with kind image or video (send_file or a script's `calvin-send-file`); the Bash call it was posted from is a render by that fact. It starts at the first render since the turn's previous visual: a Bash call whose `command_kinds` say browser or media (Playwright, ffmpeg, mermaid…), or the posting call itself when nothing earlier was recognised. The start is a heuristic from the command's head word (`node shot.mjs` says nothing); the end is exact. Failed launches, installs and retries after the start count; the model's planning before it does not. Renders with no visual after them in the turn are `abandoned`. Runners before calvin#60 report neither fact, so their turns have no rows.

TOKEN "calvin_read" READ

NODE visual_turns
DESCRIPTION >
    Per turn: when visuals landed (and from which call), when each render and install call started.

SQL >
    SELECT
        turn_id,
        anyIf(trace_id, event_name = 'turn.started') AS trace_id,
        any(session_key) AS session_key,
        any(org_id) AS org_id,
        anyIf(path, event_name = 'turn.started') AS path,
        max(synthetic) AS synthetic,
        arraySort(groupArrayIf(occurred_at, event_name = 'file.posted' AND JSONExtractString(data, 'kind') IN ('image', 'video'))) AS files,
        groupArrayIf(tool_call_id, event_name = 'file.posted' AND JSONExtractString(data, 'kind') IN ('image', 'video') AND tool_call_id != '') AS posting_calls,
        groupArrayIf((tool_call_id, occurred_at), event_name = 'model.block_started' AND tool_call_id != '') AS calls,
        groupArrayIf(
            (tool_call_id, splitByChar(',', JSONExtractString(data, 'command_kinds'))),
            event_name = 'tool.completed' AND JSONHas(data, 'command_kinds')
        ) AS kinds,
        arrayFilter(
            r -> r > toDateTime64(0, 3),
            arrayMap(k -> arrayFirst(c -> c.1 = k.1, calls).2, arrayFilter(k -> hasAny(k.2, ['browser', 'media']), kinds))
        ) AS tagged,
        arrayFilter(r -> r > toDateTime64(0, 3), arrayMap(id -> arrayFirst(c -> c.1 = id, calls).2, posting_calls)) AS posting,
        arraySort(arrayDistinct(arrayConcat(tagged, posting))) AS renders,
        arraySort(arrayFilter(
            r -> r > toDateTime64(0, 3),
            arrayMap(k -> arrayFirst(c -> c.1 = k.1, calls).2, arrayFilter(k -> has(k.2, 'install'), kinds))
        )) AS installs
    FROM
        (
            SELECT turn_id, trace_id, session_key, org_id, path, synthetic, event_name, occurred_at, tool_call_id, data
            FROM calvin_events
            WHERE service_name = 'runner' AND turn_id != ''
              AND event_name IN ('turn.started', 'model.block_started', 'tool.completed', 'file.posted')
            LIMIT 1 BY event_id
        )
    GROUP BY turn_id
    HAVING length(renders) > 0

NODE episodes
DESCRIPTION >
    One row per episode: the turn's visuals cut it into windows (previous visual, this visual]; the last window, after the last visual, ends with none.

SQL >
    SELECT
        turn_id,
        trace_id,
        session_key,
        org_id,
        path,
        synthetic,
        rs[1] AS started_at,
        posted_at,
        if(posted_at IS NULL, 'abandoned', 'posted') AS outcome,
        if(posted_at IS NULL, NULL, dateDiff('millisecond', rs[1], assumeNotNull(posted_at))) AS visual_ms,
        length(rs) AS renders,
        length(arrayFilter(x -> x >= rs[1] AND (posted_at IS NULL OR x <= assumeNotNull(posted_at)), installs)) AS installs
    FROM
        (
            SELECT
                turn_id, trace_id, session_key, org_id, path, synthetic, installs,
                arrayFilter(r -> r > w.1 AND (w.2 IS NULL OR r <= assumeNotNull(w.2)), renders) AS rs,
                w.2 AS posted_at
            FROM visual_turns
            ARRAY JOIN
                arrayMap(
                    i -> (
                        if(i = 1, toDateTime64(0, 3), files[i - 1]),
                        if(i <= length(files), toNullable(files[i]), CAST(NULL, 'Nullable(DateTime64(3))'))
                    ),
                    range(1, length(files) + 2)
                ) AS w
        )
    WHERE length(rs) > 0
